[Unit]
# The handle the compositor has on graphical-session.target, which it is not
# allowed to touch directly: that target sets RefuseManualStart, so the only
# way to bring it up is to start something bound to it. On a system with a
# display manager this is that manager's job; a compositor started from a TTY
# has nobody to do it.
#
# It matters because xdg-desktop-portal 1.22 guards its unit with
#
#   Requisite=graphical-session.target
#
# and a requisite that is inactive fails the job rather than pulling it in.
# The portal frontend then never starts, every Settings read fails, and each
# application falls back to a light theme with nothing in any log naming the
# reason.
Description=Viewport compositor session
BindsTo=graphical-session.target
Wants=graphical-session-pre.target
After=graphical-session-pre.target
